𝟕 𝐒𝐭𝐞𝐩𝐬 𝐅𝐨𝐫 𝐂𝐈/𝐂𝐃: 𝐇𝐨𝐰 𝐂𝐨𝐝𝐞 𝐆𝐨𝐞𝐬 𝐋𝐢𝐯𝐞

𝐂𝐈/𝐂𝐃 is how your idea becomes a real thing - 𝐋𝐈𝐕𝐄 in production - without breaking stuff.

Here’s how most modern teams move fast without burning the house down:

1️⃣ 𝐏𝐥𝐚𝐧
Whether it’s Jira or just sticky notes - everyone agrees what’s being built. If you skip this, welcome to chaos.

2️⃣ 𝐂𝐨𝐝𝐞
Dev time. Usually GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket. Feature branches, commits, and lots of caffeine 😅.

3️⃣ 𝐁𝐮𝐢𝐥𝐝
This is where your code gets compiled, packaged, or containerised. If it doesn’t build, it’s not going anywhere.

4️⃣ 𝐓𝐞𝐬𝐭
Automated unit, integration, and end-to-end tests. If you’re not testing here, you’re testing in prod (and praying lol).

5️⃣ 𝐑𝐞𝐥𝐞𝐚𝐬𝐞
CI hands off to CD. This is where tools like ArgoCD, Jenkins or GitHub Actions get your code ready to deploy.

6️⃣ 𝐃𝐞𝐩𝐥𝐨𝐲
This is where stuff gets real. Your image hits prod. Whether it’s Kubernetes, Lambda, or plain old VMs - you ship it.

7️⃣ 𝐌𝐨𝐧𝐢𝐭𝐨𝐫
Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog etc keep watch. Alerts get sent. Dashboards tell you what’s up. Your job’s not done till you’re sure it’s actually working.

That’s CI/CD done properly.
